d 'FINEGRAY': module for fast Fine-Gray competing risks regression
d
d  finegray fits the Fine and Gray (1999) subdistribution hazard
d model for competing risks data, reporting subdistribution hazard
d ratios for the cumulative incidence of a cause of interest. It
d uses a native Mata forward-backward scan and never expands the
d data, so it scales to large risk sets. Data are declared with
d stset; compete() names the event-type variable and cause() the
d event of interest. Supported are delayed entry, censoring and
d entry strata, a stratified baseline subdistribution hazard,
d piecewise-constant time-varying effects, factor variables with
d margins support, sampling and frequency weights, mi estimate, and
d robust, nuisance-adjusted or cluster-robust standard errors.
d Postestimation provides finegray_predict (linear predictor,
d cumulative incidence, Schoenfeld residuals, baseline hazard),
d finegray_cif (cumulative incidence at chosen covariate profiles,
d with analytic or bootstrap confidence limits), and
d finegray_phtest (proportional subdistribution hazards
d diagnostic). Methods and formulas are documented in help
d finegray_methods. 
d
d KW: competing risks
d KW: Fine-Gray
d KW: subdistribution hazard
d KW: cumulative incidence
d KW: survival analysis
d KW: delayed entry
d KW: left truncation
d KW: inverse probability of censoring weighting
d KW: st
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260909
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
f finegray.ado
